5\t<td id=\"S3.T2.1.30.28.10\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb\"><span id=\"S3.T2.1.30.28.10.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:90%;\">–</span></td>\n906\t<td id=\"S3.T2.1.30.28.11\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb\"><span id=\"S3.T2.1.30.28.11.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:90%;\">88.55</span></td>\n907\t<td id=\"S3.T2.1.30.28.12\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb\"><span id=\"S3.T2.1.30.28.12.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:90%;\">88.99</span></td>\n908\t<td id=\"S3.T2.1.30.28.13\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb\"><span id=\"S3.T2.1.30.28.13.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:90%;\">–</span></td>\n909\t</tr>\n910\t</tbody>\n911\t</table>\n912\t</figure>\n913\t<section id=\"S3.SS1\" class=\"ltx_subsection\">\n914\t<h3 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection\">\n915\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection\">3.1 </span>Further Finetuning on Low-resource Languages</h3>\n916\t\n917\t<div id=\"S3.SS1.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n918\t<p id=\"S3.SS1.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Although the proposed pipeline demonstrates broad linguistic coverage, its performance is strongly dependent on the quantity and quality of available data per language, as well as the quality of the speech encoder and the LLM. This dependency extends beyond the projector training to encompass the datasets used to train both the speech encoder and the LLM.\n919\tMonolingual systems tend to outperform their multilingual counterparts, but training them from scratch is rarely feasible for low-resource languages <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<span class=\"ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self\">fong25_interspeech</span>]</cite>. MEUSLI provides an effective starting point to improve the performance of monolingual systems as shown in Figure <a href=\"#S3.F2\" title=\"Figure 2 ‣ 3.1 Further Finetuning on Low-resource Languages ‣ 3 Results and Discussion ‣ MEUSLI: a Multilingual Projector for LLM-based ASR and Beyond\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">2</span></a>. We illustrate this using Breton (BR) and Maltese (MT) as study case using <em id=\"S3.SS1.p1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">EuroLLM 1.7B-Instruct</em>, which showed high error rates in the multilingual setting (Table <a href=\"#S3.T2\" title=\"Table 2 ‣ 3 Results and Discussion ‣ MEUSLI: a Multilingual Projector for LLM-based ASR and Beyond\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">2</span></a>).</p>\n920\t</div>\n921\t<div id=\"S3.SS1.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n922\t<p id=\"S3.SS1.p2.3\" class=\"ltx_p\">We fine-tuned the multilingual projector to a single language using, respectively: <math id=\"S3.SS1.p2.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\sim\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sim</annotation></semantics></math>18 hours of MT data from CV 20.0, FL, and MASRI-Headset v2  <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<span class=\"ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self\">Williams2023TheAO</span>]</cite> and <math id=\"S3.SS1.p2.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\sim\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sim</annotation></semantics></math>2.5 hours of BR data from CV 20.0. Training used the same setup as in Section <a href=\"#S2.SS2\" title=\"2.2 Training Configuration ‣ 2 MEUSLI: a Multilingual Projector for 28 EU Languages (and Beyond) ‣ MEUSLI: a Multilingual Projector for LLM-based ASR and Beyond\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">2.2</span></a> with a <math id=\"S3.SS1.p2.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"1\\times 10^{-4}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace=\"0.222em\" rspace=\"0.222em\">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> learning rate, batch size 4, and 10 epochs. To test if language-specific features help, we also replaced the vanilla <span id=\"S3.SS1.p2.3.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">Whisper-large-v3-turbo</span> encoder with pre-fine-tuned and better performing versions for MT<span id=\"footnote2\" class=\"ltx_note ltx_role_footnote\"><sup class=\"ltx_note_mark\">2</sup><span class=\"ltx_note_outer\"><span class=\"ltx_note_content\"><sup class=\"ltx_note_mark\">2</sup><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_note\">2</span><a href=\"https://huggingface.co/carlosdanielhernandezmena/whisper-largev2-maltese-8k-steps-64h\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter\">https://huggingface.co/carlosdanielhernandezmena/whisper-largev2-maltese-8k-steps-64h</a></span></span></span> and BR<span id=\"footnote3\" class=\"ltx_note ltx_role_footnote\"><sup class=\"ltx_note_mark\">3</sup><span class=\"ltx_note_outer\"><span class=\"ltx_note_content\"><sup class=\"ltx_note_mark\">3</sup><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_note\">3</span><a href=\"https://huggingface.co/Bretagne/whisper-large-v3-turbo-audio_breton-transcription_breton\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter\">https://huggingface.co/Bretagne/whisper-large-v3-turbo-audio_breton-transcription_breton</a></span></span></span>. Table <a href=\"#S3.T3\" title=\"Table 3 ‣ 3.1 Further Finetuning on Low-resource Languages ‣ 3 Results and Discussion ‣ MEUSLI: a Multilingual Projector for LLM-based ASR and Beyond\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">3</span></a> presents a comparative analysis between: (i) fine-tuning our pretrained multilingual projector (MEUSLI), and (ii) training a monolingual system from scratch. The results indicate that initializing with our multilingual model results in substantial performance improvements for both languages.\n923\tMoreover, MEUSLI remains beneficial even when paired with a specialized monolingual encoder. In the case of BR, the pairing outperforms systems that rely on training a dedicated monolingual projector from scratch. It, moreover, remains competitive despite BR being unsupported by EuroLLM, highlighting the pipeline's robustness in low-resource settings.</p>\n924\t</div>\n925\t<figure id=\"S3.F2\" class=\"ltx_figure\"><img src=\"2607.22100v1/figures/meusli_ft_bootstrap_fig.png\" id=\"S3.F2.g1\" class=\"ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape\" width=\"539\" height=\"115\" alt=\"Refer to caption\">\n926\t<figcaption class=\"ltx_caption ltx_centering\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure\">Figure 2: </span>Illustration of the MEUSLI fine-tuning and bootstrapping pipeline for expanding language coverage.</figcaption>\n927\t</figure>\n928\t<figure id=\"S3.T3\" class=\"ltx_table\">\n929\t<figcaption class=\"ltx_caption\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_table\">Table 3: </span><span id=\"S3.T3.3.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">Low-resource</span>: WER when fine-tuning on Breton\n930\t(BR) and Maltese (MT). Training data: CV for BR; CV, FL, and MASRI-Headsetv2 for MT. ``Mono\" refers to a monolingual projector trained on the aforementioned data, ``MEUSLI\" is our projector, ``→” indicates MEUSLI fine-tuned. Encoder `Adapt' means a pre-fine-tuned and better performing Whisper encoder was used for either MT and BR. The LLM is <em id=\"S3.T3.4.2\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">EuroLLM 1.7B-Instruct</em>.</figcaption>\n931\t<div id=\"S3.T3.5\" class=\"ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer\" style=\"width:433.6pt;height:90.3pt;vertical-align:-41.4pt;\"><span class=\"ltx_transformed_inner\" style=\"transform:translate(70.8pt,-14.7pt) scale(1.48499897447421,1.48499897447421) ;\">\n932\t<table id=\"S3.T3.5.1\" class=\"ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle\">\n933\t<thead class=\"ltx_thead\">\n934\t<tr id=\"S3.T3.5.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n935\t<th id=\"S3.T3.5.1.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r\">Lang.</th>\n936\t<th id=\"S3.T3.5.1.1.1.2\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r\">Train.</th>\n937\t<th id=\"S3.T3.5.1.1.1.3\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r\">Encoder</th>\n938\t<th id=\"S3.T3.5.1.1.1.4\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r\">Mono</th>\n939\t<th id=\"S3.T3.5.1.1.1.5\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r\">MEUSLI</th>\n940\t<th id=\"S3.T3.5.1.1.1.6\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column\">MEUSLI→</th>\n941\t</tr>\n942\t</thead>\n943\t<tbody class=\"ltx_tbody\">\n944\t<tr id=\"S3.T3.5.1.2.1\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n945\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t\" rowspan=\"2\"><span id=\"S3.T3.5.1.2.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Breton</span></td>\n946\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.2.1.2\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t\" rowspan=\"2\"><span id=\"S3.T3.5.1.2.1.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">2.5h</span></td>\n947\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.2.1.3\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t\">Large-V3</td>\n948\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.2.1.4\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t\">84.3%</td>\n949\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.2.1.5\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t\">95.7%</td>\n950\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.2.1.6\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t\"><span id=\"S3.T3.5.1.2.1.6.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">79.7%</span></td>\n951\t</tr>\n952\t<tr id=\"S3.T3.5.1.3.2\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n953\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.3.2.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r\">Adapt</td>\n954\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.3.2.2\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r\">27.7%</td>\n955\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.3.2.3\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r\">-</td>\n956\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.3.2.4\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center\"><span id=\"S3.T3.5.1.3.2.4.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">24.5%</span></td>\n957\t</tr>\n958\t<tr id=\"S3.T3.5.1.4.3\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n959\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.4.3.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t\" rowspan=\"2\"><span id=\"S3.T3.5.1.4.3.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Maltese</span></td>\n960\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.4.3.2\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t\" rowspan=\"2\"><span id=\"S3.T3.5.1.4.3.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">18h</span></td>\n961\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.4.3.3\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t\">Large-V3</td>\n962\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.4.3.4\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t\">45.8%</td>\n963\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.4.3.5\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t\">58.8%</td>\n964\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.4.3.6\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t\"><span id=\"S3.T3.5.1.4.3.6.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">39.4%</span></td>\n965\t</tr>\n966\t<tr id=\"S3.T3.5.1.5.4\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n967\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.5.4.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r\">Adapt</td>\n968\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.5.4.2\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r\"><span id=\"S3.T3.5.1.5.4.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">18.0%</span></td>\n969\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.5.4.3\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r\">-</td>\n970\t<td id=\"S3.T3.5.1.5.4.4\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_center\">23.7%</td>\n971\t</tr>\n972\t</tbody>\n973\t</table>\n974\t</span></div>\n975\t</figure>\n976\t<figure id=\"S3.T4\" class=\"ltx_table\">\n977\t<figcaption class=\"ltx_caption ltx_centering\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_table\">Table 4: </span><span id=\"S3.T4.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">Beyond 28</span>: WER for the bootstrapping experiment on Ukranian and Albanian. The training data comes from CV. ``Mono\" refers to a monoligual projector trained on the CV data, ``→\" indicates MEUSLI fine-tuned on CV data. Note that both languages are not covered by EuroLLM.</figcaption>\n978\t<table id=\"S3.T4.3\" class=\"ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle\">\n979\t<thead class=\"ltx_thead\">\n